    <version>0.18.0</version>
    <time>1786543946</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update to 0.18.0

Upstream minor release. The API surface is purely additive: an AST diff over
the whole module tree shows no public symbols removed and 18 added. One new
runtime dependency, psutil, is added to Requires; no existing floor moved.

Please take this together with python-vllm 0.27.1, submitted alongside it.
python-vllm previously carried an exact &quot;= 0.17.1&quot; requirement on this
package, which would have made it uninstallable the moment 0.18.0 landed;
that companion submission replaces the exact pin with a floor, so the two are
compatible in either order once both are in.

For the record on that pairing: vLLM upstream still pins compressed-tensors
== 0.17.0 on both v0.27.1 and main, so upstream has not itself adopted
0.18.0. All 15 symbols vllm imports from compressed_tensors were checked and
are present in both 0.17.1 and 0.18.0, with no removals, so the mismatch is a
version string rather than an API break.

There is still no %check. The previous comment justified that by saying
transformers was absent from Factory, which is no longer true; the real
reason is that python-torch is disabled on aarch64, so an import smoke test
would turn this noarch package into a build failure on every other
architecture. The comment now says so.

Verified on aarch64: build green, rpmlint 0 errors / 0 badness.</comment>
    <requestid>1370784</requestid>
  </revision>
</revisionlist>
